      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The base alloy forms multiple primary or non-eutectic crystalline phases during solidification.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::019::4_discussion",
        "PMC11642357::web::021::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The base alloy exhibits a complex, multistep crystallization sequence.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::017::4_discussion",
        "PMC11642357::web::020::4_discussion",
        "PMC11642357::web::021::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slow cooling of the base alloy produces an extensively crystalline, multiphase microstructure.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::020::4_discussion",
        "PMC11642357::web::021::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reheating of the base alloy produces extensive primary crystallization and reduced glass retention.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::017::4_discussion",
        "PMC11642357::web::021::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Very rapid cooling by melt-spinning can produce an amorphous Cr16Mn16Fe16Co16Ni16P20 ribbon.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::018::4_discussion",
        "PMC11642357::web::021::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed intervention is to add approximately 1–3 at.% Nb to the base alloy.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nb atoms will segregate at incipient crystalline nuclei in the modified alloy.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Segregated Nb will modify the local atomic environments around incipient nuclei.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nb-induced disruption of the atomic rearrangements required for primary-phase formation will increase the nucleation barrier.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The increased nucleation barrier will retard crystallization kinetics and inhibit primary non-eutectic phases.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nb addition will produce a higher amorphous phase fraction than in the base alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nb addition will enhance the thermal stability of the amorphous alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nb addition will raise the DSC crystallization-onset temperature by approximately 20–30 °C relative to the base alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The relevant melt-spinning cooling-rate boundary is approximately 10^5–10^6 K/s.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::018::4_discussion",
        "PMC11642357::web::021::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "A slower-cooling boundary is approximately 52 K/s on a copper plate.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::020::4_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cooling rate strongly changes the phase content and transformation temperatures of the base alloy.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::017::4_discussion",
        "PMC11642357::web::020::4_discussion",
        "PMC11642357::web::021::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The beneficial effects of Nb should occur under both very rapid and slower cooling conditions.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "DSC reheating can define the crystallization window used to compare thermal stability.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::017::4_discussion",
        "PMC11642357::web::021::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    }
  ],
